For STM32 GPIOX->MODER, each pin gets 2 bits.
All 32 bits in MODER Register get assigned to PX0 to PX15.

For instance, GPIOA Port:

PINS  MODER Bits      Shifts       Clear Expression
PA0	-> [1:0]     		0			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 0); 3 in Binary: 11
PA1	-> [3:2]			2			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 2);
PA2	-> [5:4]			4			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 4);
PA3	-> [7:6]			6			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 6);
PA4	-> [9:8]			8			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 8);
PA5	-> [11:10]			10			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 10);
PA6	-> [13:12]			12			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 12);
PA7	-> [15:14]			14			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 14);
PA8	-> [17:16]			16			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 16);
PA9	-> [19:18]			18			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 18);
PA10-> [21:20]			20			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 20);
PA11-> [23:22]			22			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 22);
PA12-> [25:24]			24			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 24);
PA13-> [27:26]			26			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 26);
PA14-> [29:28]			28			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 28);
PA15-> [31:30]			30 			GPIOA->MODER &= ~(3U << 30);

